      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Forty one patients were implanted DDD pacemakers (3 cases DDDR) from August, 1983 to July, 1990. 32 males and 9 females. The mean age was 62.3 years (range 32 to 91). 19 patients had coronary artery disease. The indication for pacing was II degrees-III degrees AV block in 16 patients and sick sinus syndrome in 25 patients. During follow-up period there were 2 patients had displacement, 4 patients had undersensing, 3 patients had pacemaker-mediated tachycardia and 3 patients had crosstalk. That was corrected through external programmer. The experience of this operation was discussed."},
